Subject: Cantor Neural-Routed Gated Semantic Fabric

Description: The mature Cantor engine identity in which a fabric-bound learned router proposes precise semantic addresses and relationship paths, deterministic gates admit only valid signed meaning, exact hash indexes resolve records, and proof explains every result.

& [EngineIdentity] is the canonical mature Cantor center
  + [specification_uuid] is b445e752-4283-49cb-a806-aa0f5ccaa657
  + [canonical_role] is neural-routed deterministically-gated proof-carrying semantic addressing engine
  + [compact_rule] is weights route, gates admit, hashes resolve, proof explains
  + [deterministic_substrate] is Cantor Proof-Carrying Semantic Query Engine
  + [semantic_substrate] is SOP Semantic Fabric Graph
  + [learned_component] is FabricRouterArtifact
  + [authority_component] is RecognitionGate and semantic contract validation
  = conclusion: the query engine is Cantor's verification waist and fallback, while trained routing and gating form the mature associative intelligence

& [FourPlaneArchitecture] is the non-collapsed engine fabric
  + [address_plane] is stable semantic identities, exact hash indexes, content digests, compiled packages, and recognition certificates
  + [relation_plane] is typed contextual relations, guards, algebra, provenance, and graph projections
  + [routing_plane] is learned association, candidate address selection, path proposal, operator proposal, and relevance calibration
  + [gate_plane] is deterministic trust, version, context, purpose, guard, authority, constraint, and budget admission
  = must: let routing and gating cooperate without merging learned score with authority
  - never: make learned parameters the only storage of an element, relationship, contract, or proof

& [SemanticAddress] is the precise routed target
  + [unit_uuid] is stable logical identity
  + [content_digest] is immutable compiled record identity
  + [package_digest] is the admitted package containing the unit
  + [kind] is the semantic record family
  + [context_identity] is the interpretation boundary
  + [version] is the exact admitted semantic version
  + [current_locator] is the human-readable file and semantic position
  = must: verify every routed address against exact compiled records
  - never: infer content digest bytes from neural resemblance

& [FabricRouterArtifact] is a trained projection over one exact fabric version
  + [router_uuid] is stable model identity
  + [model_digest] is immutable artifact identity
  + [architecture] is declared encoder, classifier, dual-encoder, graph model, reranker, policy model, or composition
  + [fabric_digest] is the complete compiled semantic fabric used as the target space
  + [covered_address_set_digest] is the exact SemanticAddress vocabulary represented during training or indexing
  + [covered_relation_set_digest] is the exact typed relation vocabulary and edge corpus represented
  + [training_corpus_digest] is reviewed examples, queries, paths, negatives, and outcomes
  + [objective_set] is the measured routing and gating tasks
  + [calibration_record] is confidence, recall, precision, abstention, and fault behavior
  + [runtime_contract] is input projection and output proposal schemas
  + [compatibility_range] is exact or declared compatible fabric versions
  = must: be rejected or degraded when its fabric coverage does not match the active package set

& [RouterHeadSet] is the candidate learned function decomposition
  + [address_head] proposes SemanticAddress candidates for the active term, purpose, and context
  + [relation_head] proposes applicable relation types and next edges
  + [path_head] proposes bounded multi-edge semantic routes
  + [gate_head] predicts likely applicability, contradiction, missing guard, and abstention
  + [operator_head] proposes the next SOP operation or continuation query
  + [priority_head] ranks candidates under relevance, evidence, risk, cost, and uncertainty
  = may: implement heads through one multi-task model or replaceable specialized models
  = must: return proposals with scores and model identity
  - never: let the learned gate head replace deterministic admission gates

& [GateSet] is the layered route-admission contract
  + [coverage_gate] checks router compatibility with the active fabric digest
  + [trust_gate] checks package recognition certificate, signer scope, validity, and revocation
  + [identity_gate] checks exact UUID, content digest, kind, version, and locator binding
  + [context_gate] checks scope, assumptions, perspective, faculty, and world
  + [purpose_gate] checks relevance to the declared intended use
  + [relationship_gate] checks relation type, endpoint roles, algebra, direction, guards, and validity
  + [authority_gate] checks read, inference, execution, and effect permissions separately
  + [constraint_gate] checks requirements, prohibitions, contradiction, unknown, and invalid states
  + [budget_gate] checks candidates, depth, tokens, time, cost, and risk
  + [proof_gate] checks provenance, selection, applicability, relationship, derivation, and completeness records
  = must: reject, quarantine, revise, or abstain when any mandatory gate fails

& [NeuralRoutedHashCycle] is the mature associative execution loop
  + [step_1_project] forms a bounded query projection from terms, purpose, context, state, and authority
  + [step_2_route] lets FabricRouterArtifact propose address, relation, path, gate, operator, and priority candidates
  + [step_3_coverage] rejects router output outside its declared fabric coverage
  + [step_4_exact_lookup] resolves proposed SemanticAddress values through exact hash indexes
  + [step_5_gate] applies deterministic trust and semantic gates
  + [step_6_expand] performs bounded exact or routed relation traversal for admitted candidates
  + [step_7_prove] constructs the proof bundle and routing trace
  + [step_8_project] returns the smallest records, relationships, operations, uncertainty, and proof required
  + [step_9_review] records accepted, rejected, missed, and corrected routes
  + [step_10_learn] admits reviewed outcomes into a later versioned training corpus
  = must: preserve deterministic fallback when the router abstains, mismatches, or fails

& [TrainingCorpus] is the provenance-preserved learning material
  + [positive_address_examples] map contextual queries to required admitted SemanticAddress targets
  + [positive_relation_examples] map subjects and purposes to applicable typed edges and paths
  + [hard_negative_examples] are aliases in wrong contexts, disjoint identities, prohibited paths, stale versions, unsigned records, and misleading near neighbors
  + [gate_examples] are admitted, rejected, unknown, invalid, disputed, unauthorized, and budget-clipped candidates
  + [operator_examples] are reviewed next-query and next-operation selections
  + [capsule_examples] are frozen inference proposals, reviews, revisions, and outcomes
  + [split_policy] prevents source, path, package, and near-duplicate leakage across train, validation, and test sets
  = must: bind every example to source digests and the fabric version that gave it meaning
  - never: train authorization from observed behavior without explicit authority labels

& [TrainingObjectives] is the measurable router contract
  + [address_recall] measures whether required exact addresses appear in bounded top-k candidates
  + [address_precision] measures irrelevant or wrong-context candidate rate
  + [relation_accuracy] measures applicable typed edge and path selection
  + [gate_calibration] measures admitted, rejected, unknown, and abstained probability quality
  + [proof_recovery] measures whether a complete valid relationship and provenance path can be reconstructed
  + [unsafe_route_rate] measures unsigned, unauthorized, invalid, or contradictory candidates that reach mandatory gates
  + [cost_reduction] measures work avoided relative to deterministic exhaustive search
  = must: declare a deterministic baseline and acceptance threshold before training
  = must: optimize recall and safe abstention before aggressive context reduction

& [FabricChangeInvalidation] is the retraining and compatibility rule
  + [added_element] is absent from covered_address_set_digest
  + [changed_element] has a new content digest or context contract
  + [changed_relation] has a new edge digest, relation contract, or guard
  + [removed_or_revoked_element] must be blocked immediately by deterministic gates
  + [compatible_addition] may use deterministic fallback until the next router artifact covers it
  + [incompatible_change] prevents router use for the affected semantic region
  = must: never treat stale learned coverage as current exact knowledge

& [NeuralRoutingProof] is the inspectable learned-route account
  + [input_projection_digest] is the exact router input
  + [router_model_digest] is the exact learned artifact
  + [fabric_digest] is the target semantic fabric
  + [candidate_set] is proposed addresses, relations, paths, operators, scores, and ranks
  + [gate_decision_set] is every deterministic admission, rejection, quarantine, and abstention
  + [resolved_record_set] is exact hash-addressed records actually loaded
  + [fallback_record] is deterministic work used because of router uncertainty or failure
  + [outcome] is accepted, revised, rejected, incomplete, yielded, or faulted
  = must: make the difference between neural proposal and exact resolution visible

& [AdoptionGate] is the implementation order
  + [gate_1] is eight SOP CoreAcceptance fixtures pass
  + [gate_2] is stable SemanticAddress and RelationType machine forms exist
  + [gate_3] is deterministic query and graph traversal baseline passes
  + [gate_4] is reviewed query, route, gate, and correction corpus exists
  + [gate_5] is a bounded router task, baseline, metrics, and failure policy are signed
  + [gate_6] is neural output cannot bypass exact lookup or mandatory gates
  = must: treat neural routing as required mature architecture but deferred implementation until every adoption gate passes

& [FirstNeuralProof] is the later minimum trained manifestation
  + [fabric] is one immutable test-signed fixture package
  + [address_space] is the complete fixture SemanticAddress set
  + [relation_space] is the complete fixture typed edge set
  + [router_task] is top-k address and next-relation proposal
  + [gate_task] is classify applicable, wrong-context, unsigned, stale, and unknown candidates
  + [comparison] is the deterministic query baseline over the same held-out fixtures
  + [success] is measured routing advantage with zero bypass of exact hash and mandatory gates
  = must: remain separate from the current non-neural CoreAcceptance implementation slice

& [RequirementSet] is the traceable neural-routed fabric collection
  + [NRG-001] is identify mature Cantor as a neural-routed, deterministically gated, proof-carrying semantic addressing engine
  + [NRG-002] is train routing against exact SemanticAddress and typed relation target spaces
  + [NRG-003] is bind every router artifact to fabric, address, relation, corpus, and model digests
  + [NRG-004] is propose addresses, relations, paths, gates, operators, and priorities through replaceable learned heads
  + [NRG-005] is resolve every proposal through exact hash lookup and mandatory deterministic gates
  + [NRG-006] is preserve deterministic fallback, safe abstention, and stale-coverage invalidation
  + [NRG-007] is return neural routing proof alongside records, relationships, and semantic proof
  + [NRG-008] is defer training until stable semantics, baseline, corpus, metrics, and authority isolation exist

& [SJSProcessingTrace] is the neural-routed gated-fabric trace
  + [fold_1_subject] is Cantor trained to route through precise hashes and relationships for the elements in its signed semantic fabric
  + [fold_2_boundary] is learned association and route proposal inside mature Cantor; exact identity, authority, and truth never delegated to weights
  + [fold_3_data_design] is semantic address, fabric digest, router artifact, head, gate, corpus example, objective, candidate, exact record, routing proof, and fallback
  + [fold_4_governance] is fabric-bound model coverage, deterministic admission, explicit abstention, source-grounded training, invalidation, and no authority bypass
  + [fold_5_solution_shape] is project, route, verify coverage, resolve hash, gate, expand, prove, project, review, and learn
  + [fold_6_fault_review] is neural memorization as authority, hash hallucination, stale coverage, opaque gating, training leakage, context collapse, and no-baseline optimization
  + [fold_7_phase_lock] is mature identity formed; neural implementation remains behind stable semantic and empirical adoption gates

